  "body": "I'm currently developing a web app that connects to two motion sensors via the web bluetooth API. They both have the same data output rate. However, when both of them are simultaneosly measuring and sending back the data to their respective event listeners, one of them seems to send almost exactly half the amount of data. Specifically, it's always the device I connect in the first place that sends less data.  It's not an issue with the sensors, as when they are connected alone, they both send the correct amount of data.\r\n\r\nIs it posible that the navigator sets a kind of a \"priority\" on one of them and process more events generated from it because of a shortage of resources?\r\n\r\nThanks in advance!",
